<title>USA: Pharmhouse agrees to settle Woolworth litigation.</title>
<headline>Pharmhouse agrees to settle Woolworth litigation.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmhouse Corp said on Monday that it agreed in principle to settle pending litigation it initiated against a unit of Woolworth Corp over its purchase of 24 Rx Place stores from Woolworth in April 1995.</p>
<p>While the settlement was not final, the company said Woolowrth forgave debt, including $8.4 million in purchase money notes. The agreement also provided for the return of certain under-performing Rx Place stores to Woolworth during the early part of fiscal 1998. Pharmhouse said it was hoping the settlement would occur during the fiscal fourth quarter.</p>
</text>
